    "title": "Panel Unpacks $18 Billion for NYC Infrastructure Projects Being Put on Hold | NTD",
    "text": "Office of Management and Budget Director Russell Vought wrote on X on Wednesday that roughly $18 billion for New York City infrastructure projects has been put on hold. Joining NTD to discuss is Dan Turrentine, co-host of 2WAY’s \"The Morning Meeting\" and \"The Group Chat,\" along with Katie Zacharia, senior legal adviser to Fix California.\nPanel Unpacks $18 Billion for NYC Infrastructure Projects Being Put on Hold\nDan Turrentine and Katie Zacharia discussed the impact of freezing $18 billion for New York City infrastructure projects.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/1/2025, 11:25:00 PM EDT",
